    "biography": {
      "concept": "Silver dragon lounging on the frontage of the Crown Mall (Act 4)",
      "notes": "Donny is the enormous silver dragon who lounges on the frontage of the Crown Mall like the apocalypse forgot to tell him to stop having a good afternoon. He hums and blows smoke rings. He keeps out bad vibes, not people, and he pop-quizzes visitors on whether they mean to use, save or take over the mall. He is a surfer-sage ('little my dudes'), more disappointed than angry, and his advice is to try being people first. Don't make him feel stupid; he takes that in a very draconic register."
    }
